            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“If there is a dispute between men, and they come into court, and the judges decide between them, acquitting the innocent and condemning the guilty, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.25.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.25.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 25:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "then if the guilty man deserves to be beaten, the judge shall cause him to lie down and be beaten in his presence with a number of stripes in proportion to his offense. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.25.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.25.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 25:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Forty stripes may be given him, but not more; lest, if one should go on to beat him with more stripes than these, your brother be degraded in your sight.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.25.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.25.3"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
